xnu 0420: bring Venus through PAS 9 to HFI SYS_PROP (mondrianvenus=1)

The opt-in worker votes MMCX/MXC, enables the VideoCC/GCC domains and
LUCID_OLE PLL, maps the fixed firmware/queue regions, programs the two
Venus SMMU streams, loads the provenance-verified vpu20_4v.mbn through
PAS 9 and polls the IRIS2 HFI queues for INIT and IMAGE_VERSION. It
shuts PAS down and faults/disables the SMMU context after the proof.

The firmware is read from /private/var/vm/vpu20_4v.mbn and is not embedded
or committed. Stock vendor_a extraction SHA-256:
532c97f749e83906932fae6c348fe9d55ca5dd47f5b74e245c597b1fda504c9d.

Architecture follows DenialOfGravity/ios-redfin (MIT); SM8475 register and
HFI facts come from the live DT, mainline and the pinned Qualcomm vendor
driver (GPL-2.0, facts only). No GPL or vendor source is copied.

